messages:
alex: Heads-up: onboarding docs currently show require() examples for the JS SDK but our edge quickstart and samples use ESM. I'm getting repros from new users where their code fails in edge runtimes and in bundled apps. Any objections if I send a docs PR to show both patterns + a short compatibility note? :wave:
maria: Yes please — support just got a bug where a user pasted the CJS snippet into a Cloudflare Worker and it threw at import time. :thinking_face:
kevin: Quick technical note: require()ing an ESM package yields the module namespace where the default export lives on .default. So: `const r = require('@redwood/inference')` -> you often need `r.default`. That surprises folks.
sam: Also TS consumers run into typings mismatch: our d.ts exposes named exports (e.g., `export class Client`) but people copy default-import examples. That triggers `TS2707`/`TS1192` style errors.
alex: Example of what we currently show (CJS) — this is the snippet that trips people when the package is ESM-only:
```js
// CJS - problematic if package is ESM-only
const Redwood = require('@redwood/inference');
const client = new Redwood.Client({ apiKey: process.env.RW_API_KEY });
```
kevin: And the recommended ESM pattern for edge runtimes / modern bundlers:
```js
// ESM - recommended for edge runtimes
import { Client } from '@redwood/inference';
const client = new Client({ apiKey: Deno.env.get('RW_API_KEY') });
```
maria: Doc changes I'd like to see: short section that lists 3 rows: Node (CJS vs ESM support), Bundlers (esbuild/webpack/rollup notes), Edge (Cloudflare/Vercel — prefer ESM). Also add explicit minimal examples for CJS and ESM.
kevin: Also include a tiny compatibility tip for folks stuck on CJS or older Node: e.g.
```js
// Defensive CJS interop if package is ESM-built
const pkg = require('@redwood/inference');
const Client = pkg.Client || pkg.default?.Client || pkg.default || pkg;
const client = new Client({ apiKey: process.env.RW_API_KEY });
```
(not pretty but helps users quickly unblock)
sam: For TS, add examples: `import { Client } from '@redwood/inference'` and `import type { ClientOptions } from '@redwood/inference'`. Also a note about "allowSyntheticDefaultImports": true in tsconfig if they really want `import Redwood from` style.
alex: I'll open a PR that: 1) swaps the onboarding examples to show ESM first, 2) includes a CJS defensive pattern, 3) adds an FAQ blurb "why require() yields undefined/.default", and 4) a short edge bundling note (esbuild args + Vercel/CF example).
devex-bot: PR opened: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/467 — adds ESM/CJS examples, edge notes, and TS typing tips :sparkles:
maria: :thumbsup: I'll add a test snippet for Cloudflare Workers (tiny runnable example) so support can paste to repro.
kevin: Add a short line about package.json exports + main/module/exports fields so people understand why interop differs between versions of node and bundlers. Link to the exports RFC or short snippet.
alex: Nice. Can we keep the docs language very brief — people copy/paste; avoid long theory. Also add the exact CLI esbuild command in a code block so deploys are easy.
sam: One operational note: ask triage to capture Node version, bundler, and whether they deployed to an edge runtime. That info speeds debugging. :ok_hand:
alex: Cool — I'll draft the PR and ping reviewers (maria, kevin). Thanks all.
